; E168 Phase 12, G9(ii) -- MUST NOT COMPILE. THE SWAP IN THE OTHER DIRECTION.
;
; A hand-written `Expect` dropped into the `diffs` slot claims a provenance it
; does not have: `diffs` means "minted by a differential", and `gate-verdict`
; reads that claim to decide whether the rank floor applies at all. Before
; 2026-08-25 this compiled. It happened to fail CLOSED -- `best-rank` of an
; empty `checks` list is 5, so the floor fired and the gate scored inadequate --
; which is luck, not design: the same forgery beside any rank-3 check would have
; cleared the floor on an anchor that was never independent of anything.
;
; Both directions are refused by the same type now. G9(i) is the direction that
; failed OPEN; this is the one that failed closed for the wrong reason.
;
; The compiling twin is e168_rank_floor.chiral, whose `fixed-check` and
; `meaning-check` are hand-written and stay in `checks`, where a hand-written
; expectation belongs.
;
; want: exit 1, `load: type mismatch`

(import "evidence/test-floor")

(def killed MutRun (mu-killed "a mutant that ran and died" (ob-exit 42) (ob-exit 41)))

(def hand Expect
  (ex (obk-given "written by hand, not minted by a differential")
      (ob-exit 41)
      (pv-meaning "the source returns 41, so the process exits 41")))

(def forged Gate
  (gate "markers agree" (the (List Expect) nil) (cons hand nil) killed))

(def compile-main (-> I64 I64) (lam (n) 0))
